{"id": "sevt_01FWmnVDBD8SkqJk1du1zf1V", "content": [{"text": "**No, auth isn't the problem. The cause is the checkout deploy `a3f9c21`, which went out at 14:31:18.**\n\n**Timeline**\n- **14:31:** checkout p99 jumps from about 75 ms to about 3,850 ms. That is the same minute as the deploy, so the onset is 14:31, not 14:32. It keeps climbing to about 5,000 ms by 14:59.\n- **14:31 to 14:40:** checkout `db_pool_utilization` climbs steadily from 0.2 and hits 1.0 at 14:40.\n- **14:40 onward:** checkout `error_rate` starts at 0.23 and stays at 0.1 to 0.67. That is pool exhaustion, which comes after the latency spike rather than causing it.\n\n**Why auth is ruled out**\n- Auth p99 stays flat at about 50 to 80 ms for the whole window.\n- The only auth deploy, `9f1e2d4`, was at 11:02, more than 3 hours before the spike.\n- The log does show auth errors, but they are `idp.internal` timeouts and GC pauses from 14:15, which is before the incident. Auth latency didn't move, so they aren't what is hurting checkout.\n- The inventory deploy at 14:55 came after the spike started, so it can't be the cause.\n\n**What the diff does**\n- `a3f9c21` is labelled \"refactor for readability\". It replaces one batched `OrderItem ... order_id__in` query with a query per order row inside a loop. This is an N+1 query.\n- The log confirms it. Before 14:31, checkout logs `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id IN (?)`, one query per request. From 14:31:18, it logs 3,320 `... WHERE order_id = ?` queries, starting at the deploy second on checkout-3.\n- Each request now holds a DB connection for many sequential round trips. That drives up latency and then exhausts the pool.\n\n**Fix:** revert `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched query with grouping in memory. The refactor can be redone afterwards, keeping the single query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the checkout \"readability refactor\" replaced the batched `order_items` query with one query per order row (N+1), which inflated request latency and saturated the checkout DB pool.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T06:00:46.242836Z", "type": "agent.message"}
